    "docHtml": "<p>A curved wooden throwing-stick that travels in a flat arc and strikes targets at a distance, the boomerang is a hunting tool pressed occasionally into war service. Heavy war-boomerangs do not return; they are thrown to break legs or ribs of fleeing game or skirmishers. Light returning variants are ceremonial; practical warriors keep them as backup implements.</p>\n",
